       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, if you're starting therapy or want a lower starting dose.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if the dose is intentional. I'd add a note with your rationale, such as specialist guidance or a specific indication, and I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy.\n\nIf 20 mg was a typo, for example for 2.5 mg or 10 mg, tell me the dose you meant and I'll enter it right away."
